We are getting: Booking failed (functions/internal): internal
This means the callable Cloud Function is crashing (unhandled exception).

Most likely cause:
The guest booking page calls the same callable used by logged-in users, but the function expects context.auth.uid.
In guest mode, context.auth is null, so accessing context.auth.uid throws and results in functions/internal.

Fix with the smallest, safest changes:

A) Find the real crash line
1) Open Firebase Console -> Functions -> Logs
2) Reproduce the booking, then open the latest log entry for the booking callable (e.g. createGuestAppointment / bookAppointment)
3) Identify the exact exception + line number.

B) Make the callable support Guest (no auth required)
File: functions/index.js (or functions/src/index.ts)
1) Wrap the callable body with try/catch.
2) DO NOT access context.auth.uid unless it exists.
   Example pattern:

export const createGuestAppointment = functions.region('us-central1').https.onCall(async (data, context) => {
  try {
    const uid = context?.auth?.uid || null; // allow guest
    // Validate required fields from data:
    // fullName, phone, date/time, topic, etc
    if (!data?.fullName || !data?.phone || !data?.slotId) {
      throw new functions.https.HttpsError('invalid-argument', 'Missing required fields');
    }

    // When saving appointment, store:
    // userId: uid (nullable)
    // isGuest: !uid
    // guestEmail/guestPhone/fullName
    // createdAt serverTimestamp
    // IMPORTANT: write to the SAME collection/table used by normal appointments
    // so it appears in the same appointments schedule.

    // Return success object { ok: true, appointmentId: ... }
  } catch (e) {
    console.error('createGuestAppointment crash', e);
    // Convert unknown errors to a readable HttpsError:
    if (e instanceof functions.https.HttpsError) throw e;
    throw new functions.https.HttpsError('internal', 'Booking failed (server error). Please retry.');
  }
});

C) Client: keep friendly UI message, but log details
File: the booking page (PublicBooking.tsx / BookAppointment.tsx)
- In catch(err): console.error(err)
- Show user-friendly error (no raw code in production)

D) Do NOT change UI layout, routing, or any other booking logic.

Return ONLY the updated function file (and the booking page file if you changed the error message).

