Fix public appointment booking failing with "(functions/internal): internal" in Firebase callable createGuestAppointment.

Likely cause:
Firestore query inside the Cloud Function uses 2 where filters (dateKey + status) which can require a composite index and fails inside Functions, returning internal.

Make the smallest safe fix: remove the compound Firestore query and do filtering in code.

File: functions/index.js
Function: exports.createGuestAppointment

Change ONLY the conflict-check query part:

Current code:
  const conflictQuery = await db.collection('appointment_bookings')
    .where('dateKey', '==', dateKey)
    .where('status', '==', 'confirmed')
    .get();

Replace with:
  const daySnap = await db.collection('appointment_bookings')
    .where('dateKey', '==', dateKey)
    .get();

Then, when checking conflicts, only consider bookings with status in ['confirmed','pending'] (or at least 'confirmed'), and guard timestamp parsing safely:

  daySnap.forEach(doc => {
    const b = doc.data();

    const status = b.status;
    if (status !== 'confirmed' && status !== 'pending') return;

    const s = b.startAt?.toMillis ? b.startAt.toMillis() : null;
    const e = b.endAt?.toMillis ? b.endAt.toMillis() : null;
    if (!s || !e) return; // skip malformed docs safely

    if (startAtMs < e && endAtMs > s) conflict = true;
  });

Do NOT change any other logic, UI, or payload fields.
Keep existing error handling and success return.
Return the updated functions/index.js only.

