Fix the booking failure (functions/internal: internal) in the guest appointment booking callable.

Root cause:
In Cloud Functions, createGuestAppointment checks conflicts by calling booking.startAt.toMillis() and booking.endAt.toMillis().
If there are legacy confirmed bookings that don't have startAt/endAt as Firestore Timestamp (missing, number, string, etc.), the function crashes and the client sees functions/internal.

Implement the simplest safe fix:
- Only edit the conflict-check loop in: functions/index.js
- Do NOT change the UI, routing, or any other logic.

Steps:

1) Open: functions/index.js
2) Find this block right after:
   const snapshot = await conflictQuery.get();

It currently looks like:
  let hasConflict = false;
  snapshot.forEach(doc => {
    const booking = doc.data();
    const bookStart = booking.startAt.toMillis();
    const bookEnd = booking.endAt.toMillis();

    if (bookStart < endAtMs && bookEnd > startAtMs) {
      hasConflict = true;
    }
  });

3) Replace the entire block above with this safer version:

  const toMillisSafe = (v) => {
    if (!v) return null;
    if (typeof v === 'number') return v;
    if (typeof v === 'string') {
      const n = Number(v);
      if (!Number.isNaN(n)) return n;
      const t = Date.parse(v);
      if (!Number.isNaN(t)) return t;
      return null;
    }
    if (typeof v.toMillis === 'function') return v.toMillis();
    if (typeof v._seconds === 'number') {
      return v._seconds * 1000 + Math.floor((v._nanoseconds || 0) / 1e6);
    }
    return null;
  };

  let hasConflict = false;
  snapshot.forEach((docSnap) => {
    if (hasConflict) return;

    const booking = docSnap.data() || {};
    let bookStart = toMillisSafe(booking.startAt);
    let bookEnd = toMillisSafe(booking.endAt);

    // Fallback for legacy records: build from dateKey + time if available
    if (bookStart == null || bookEnd == null) {
      const legacyIso = (booking.dateKey && booking.time)
        ? `${booking.dateKey}T${booking.time}:00+03:00`
        : null;

      const legacyStart = legacyIso ? new Date(legacyIso).getTime() : NaN;

      if (!Number.isNaN(legacyStart)) {
        const legacyDuration = Number(booking.durationMin || durationMin) || durationMin;
        bookStart = legacyStart;
        bookEnd = legacyStart + legacyDuration * 60 * 1000;
      } else {
        console.warn(`Skipping booking ${docSnap.id}: missing/invalid startAt/endAt`);
        return;
      }
    }

    if (bookStart < endAtMs && bookEnd > startAtMs) {
      hasConflict = true;
    }
  });

4) Do not touch anything else.
5) Redeploy functions.

Return the updated functions/index.js file only.

